/// The India Post emblem, base64 PNG, for the official report letterhead.
///
/// Kept as a Dart constant rather than a bundled asset on purpose: a new file
/// under `assets/` changes the APK and would force a full Shorebird RELEASE,
/// which means the agent reinstalling. A base64 string is Dart code, so it
/// ships as an ordinary OTA patch. `lib/assets_b64.dart` already does this for
/// the app's own logo.
///
/// EMPTY until the artwork is added — [hasIndiaPostEmblem] is what the report
/// checks, and with no image the letterhead falls back to the text-only form
/// it has always used. Nothing breaks; the emblem is simply absent.
///
/// To fill it: put the PNG at `tool/india_post_logo.png` and run
/// `dart run tool/embed_emblem.dart`, which rewrites this constant.
///
/// Keep it small. This string is compiled into the app and rides in every
/// patch — a 200 KB PNG is 270 KB of base64 in the binary, for a mark printed
/// about 40pt wide. 400px on the long edge is plenty.
const String indiaPostEmblemBase64 = '';

bool get hasIndiaPostEmblem => indiaPostEmblemBase64.isNotEmpty;
